From 1ddc88f4c520d96e9e2af84c7ab5d7ccb37240c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 03:36:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Find the CPU temperature on Rockchip and similar SoCs

The hwmon sensor is looked up by name against a fixed list, and an SoC
whose thermal zones are named after what they sit next to is not on it.
An RK3588 board exposes package_thermal, littlecore_thermal and the
bigcore zones, so System information shows no temperature at all.

Add those names along with soc_thermal, which the earlier Rockchip SoCs
use. The zone covering the whole package comes first in sysfs, so that is
the one picked up.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 xbmc/platform/linux/CPUInfoLinux.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/xbmc/platform/linux/CPUInfoLinux.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/platform/linux/CPUInfoLinux.cpp
@@ -102,6 +102,12 @@ CCPUInfoLinux::CCPUInfoLinux()
       "scpi_sensors",
       "imx_thermal_zone",
       "cpu_thermal",
+      "soc_thermal",
+      "package_thermal",
+      "littlecore_thermal",
+      "bigcore0_thermal",
+      "bigcore1_thermal",
+      "bigcore2_thermal",
   });
 
   for (int i = 0; i < 20; i++)
